Weight heterogeneity at fixed raw support
n = 6000, target median raw support = 60, permutations per profile = 200, seed = 20261109

profile       b    n_B    ESS  sd(CEQ) sd(CEQ2) sd*sqrtESS    rel.sd
--------------------------------------------------------------------
binary   0.0272     60  124.0   0.0029   0.0027    0.0321    0.0029
gauss    0.0272     60   54.4   0.0035   0.0014    0.0258    0.0035
sharp    0.0272     60   14.3   0.0060   0.0047    0.0225    0.0060
jitter   0.0272     60   14.9   0.0096   0.0093    0.0370    0.0096

sd(CEQ) rises by a factor of about 3.3 across profiles while the raw
support is identical; sd*sqrt(ESS) stays roughly constant, so the variance
scale is the effective sample size and not the non-zero count.

